\tag{fdip}
\title{Interacting transfer on a finite spatial graph}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The [Gaussian time chain](fdip-007S) transfers a single field
coordinate between adjacent times. A spatial chain has a whole
configuration at each time: neighboring sites are coupled, and an
onsite quartic changes the Gaussian weight. How can one transfer
these configurations while retaining positive operators, exact
periodic probabilities and [temporal reflection positivity](fdip-007M)?}

\p{The heat kernel and the half-potential factors give the same
operator pattern as the Gaussian construction. The
onsite reflection decomposition of \ref{fdip-007O} and the trace-square
argument of \ref{fdip-0086} apply to entire spatial slices. Counting
coordinates fix all volumes and heat-kernel constants.}

